`norm()`: lowercase → أ/إ/آ→ا → ة→ه → ى→ي → strip leading ال → collapse spaces; then an alias index per city (عربي + English). Lives in the tested sales-geo engine; `npx vitest run src/engine/fusion/sales/sales-geo-engine.test.ts` passed 4/4 in this container.
const norm = s => s.toLowerCase().trim()
  .replace(/[أإآ]/g, 'ا').replace(/ة/g, 'ه').replace(/ى/g, 'ي')
  .replace(/^ال/, '').replace(/\s+/g, ' ');

Turf: `greatCircle(from,to,{npoints:100})`; if it splits at the antimeridian keep the longest segment; `length()` in km; per frame `lineSliceAlong(route, 0, max(0.001, len*progress))` into a GeoJSON source. Travel window 20 %→82 % of the shot (ease-in-out), hold the rest. For a visually straight line use a plain 2-point LineString. Without Turf: slerp on the sphere, then project with D3 into an SVG path and use `stroke-dashoffset`.
// slerp between two [lng,lat] points, t in 0..1 (no Turf needed)
const R = Math.PI / 180, v = ([lo, la]) =>
  [Math.cos(la*R)*Math.cos(lo*R), Math.cos(la*R)*Math.sin(lo*R), Math.sin(la*R)];
function gc(a, b, t) { const A = v(a), B = v(b);
  const w = Math.acos(A.reduce((s, x, i) => s + x*B[i], 0));
  const k1 = Math.sin((1-t)*w)/Math.sin(w), k2 = Math.sin(t*w)/Math.sin(w);
  const [x, y, z] = A.map((x, i) => k1*x + k2*B[i]);
  return [Math.atan2(y, x)/R, Math.asin(z)/R]; }

